## What this predicate means

**A `previous-by-date` B** — A and B are occurrents where B's temporal position precedes A's; the assertion points backward in time.  Inverse of `next-by-date` — they form a dagger pair giving bidirectional navigation through append-only chronological sequences.  Preserves all characteristics of `next-by-date` (asymmetric + irreflexive + NOT transitive) — the pairwise-cons-list invariant runs in both directions.

